---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Crisis Analysis" description="Six crisis scenarios, 17 countries analyzed, honest rankings. Where do you want to be when the assumptions stop holding?">

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="relative h-[60vh] min-h-[500px] flex items-end overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-bark-900 via-bark-800 to-bark-900"></div>
    <!-- Subtle grid pattern overlay -->
    <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.04]" style="background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(0deg, transparent, transparent 49px, rgba(255,255,255,0.5) 50px), repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, transparent 49px, rgba(255,255,255,0.5) 50px);"></div>
    <!-- Accent glow -->
    <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10" style="background-image: radial-gradient(ellipse at 30% 70%, var(--color-ember) 0%, transparent 50%), radial-gradient(ellipse at 70% 30%, var(--color-cyan) 0%, transparent 50%);"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-bark-900/95 via-bark-900/30 to-transparent"></div>
    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-10 pb-16 w-full">
      <span class="text-label text-ember tracking-[0.2em]">Crisis Analysis</span>
      <h1 class="text-display text-bark-50 mt-3 max-w-4xl text-split">Six Scenarios, One Question</h1>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-bark-300 mt-5 max-w-2xl">
        Where do you want to be when the assumptions stop holding?
        We analyzed 17 countries across 6 crisis types. Here's what we found.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Six Scenarios — Card Grid -->
  <section class="py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <div class="mb-14">
        <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 reveal">The Six Scenarios</h2>
        <p class="text-bark-500 mt-3 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="100">
          Each scenario is analyzed independently. Countries are ranked on 10 weighted factors
          &mdash; food self-sufficiency, energy independence, water security, military target risk,
          community cohesion, healthcare, economic resilience, geographic isolation, climate stability,
          and governance stability.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">

        <!-- Scenario 1: Nuclear Exchange -->
        <div class="scenario-card reveal" data-delay="0">
          <div class="scenario-icon">&#9762;</div>
          <h3 class="scenario-title">Nuclear Exchange</h3>
          <p class="scenario-desc">
            NATO/Russia or US/China escalation goes nuclear. Nuclear winter drops global temperatures
            5&ndash;10&deg;C. Agricultural productivity falls 40&ndash;97%. Over 5 billion famine deaths modeled.
          </p>
          <div class="scenario-ratings">
            <div class="scenario-rating">
              <span class="scenario-rating-label">Bolivia</span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-bar"><span class="scenario-bar-fill" style="width:65%"></span></span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-value">6.5<span class="scenario-rating-max">/10</span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="scenario-rating">
              <span class="scenario-rating-label">Yungas</span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-bar yungas"><span class="scenario-bar-fill yungas" style="width:70%"></span></span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-value accent">7.0<span class="scenario-rating-max">/10</span></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="scenario-rank">#9 of 17</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Scenario 2: Sea Logistics Collapse -->
        <div class="scenario-card reveal" data-delay="100">
          <div class="scenario-icon">&#9875;</div>
          <h3 class="scenario-title">Sea Logistics Collapse</h3>
          <p class="scenario-desc">
            Suez, Panama, or South China Sea chokepoints blockaded or destroyed. 90% of global trade moves
            by sea. Container shipping halts. Fuel, pharmaceuticals, food commodities stop flowing.
          </p>
          <div class="scenario-ratings">
            <div class="scenario-rating">
              <span class="scenario-rating-label">Bolivia</span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-bar"><span class="scenario-bar-fill" style="width:75%"></span></span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-value">7.5<span class="scenario-rating-max">/10</span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="scenario-rating">
              <span class="scenario-rating-label">Yungas</span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-bar yungas"><span class="scenario-bar-fill yungas" style="width:80%"></span></span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-value accent">8.0<span class="scenario-rating-max">/10</span></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="scenario-rank">#6 of 17</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Scenario 3: Digital Infrastructure Attack -->
        <div class="scenario-card reveal" data-delay="200">
          <div class="scenario-icon">&#9889;</div>
          <h3 class="scenario-title">Digital Infrastructure Attack</h3>
          <p class="scenario-desc">
            Undersea cables cut, satellites jammed, internet backbone compromised. Financial systems,
            supply chain coordination, and government operations fragment. $9 trillion in daily trade
            at risk.
          </p>
          <div class="scenario-ratings">
            <div class="scenario-rating">
              <span class="scenario-rating-label">Bolivia</span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-bar"><span class="scenario-bar-fill" style="width:85%"></span></span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-value">8.5<span class="scenario-rating-max">/10</span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="scenario-rating">
              <span class="scenario-rating-label">Yungas</span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-bar yungas"><span class="scenario-bar-fill yungas" style="width:90%"></span></span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-value accent">9.0<span class="scenario-rating-max">/10</span></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="scenario-rank">#1 of 17</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Scenario 4: Trust Crisis -->
        <div class="scenario-card reveal" data-delay="300">
          <div class="scenario-icon">&#128065;</div>
          <h3 class="scenario-title">Trust Crisis</h3>
          <p class="scenario-desc">
            Banks, governments, media, and currency lose legitimacy simultaneously. AI deepfakes make
            verification of any digital content impossible. Already underway &mdash; Edelman 2026 confirms
            institutional trust in freefall.
          </p>
          <div class="scenario-ratings">
            <div class="scenario-rating">
              <span class="scenario-rating-label">Bolivia</span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-bar"><span class="scenario-bar-fill" style="width:90%"></span></span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-value">9.0<span class="scenario-rating-max">/10</span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="scenario-rating">
              <span class="scenario-rating-label">Yungas</span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-bar yungas"><span class="scenario-bar-fill yungas" style="width:95%"></span></span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-value accent">9.5<span class="scenario-rating-max">/10</span></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="scenario-rank">#1 of 17</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Scenario 5: Resource Wars -->
        <div class="scenario-card reveal" data-delay="400">
          <div class="scenario-icon">&#9935;</div>
          <h3 class="scenario-title">Resource Wars</h3>
          <p class="scenario-desc">
            Water stress, lithium scarcity, and rare earth dependencies become active conflict triggers.
            Bolivia holds the world's largest lithium reserves. That makes it a target, not a haven.
          </p>
          <div class="scenario-ratings">
            <div class="scenario-rating">
              <span class="scenario-rating-label">Bolivia</span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-bar"><span class="scenario-bar-fill" style="width:50%"></span></span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-value">5.0<span class="scenario-rating-max">/10</span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="scenario-rating">
              <span class="scenario-rating-label">Yungas</span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-bar yungas"><span class="scenario-bar-fill yungas" style="width:65%"></span></span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-value accent">6.5<span class="scenario-rating-max">/10</span></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="scenario-rank">#14 of 17</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Scenario 6: Pandemic -->
        <div class="scenario-card reveal" data-delay="500">
          <div class="scenario-icon">&#129440;</div>
          <h3 class="scenario-title">Pandemic</h3>
          <p class="scenario-desc">
            A pathogen with 5&ndash;15% CFR, longer incubation, airborne transmission. No country fully
            prepared. GHSI rankings did not predict COVID outcomes &mdash; community engagement outperformed
            wealth.
          </p>
          <div class="scenario-ratings">
            <div class="scenario-rating">
              <span class="scenario-rating-label">Bolivia</span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-bar"><span class="scenario-bar-fill" style="width:50%"></span></span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-value">5.0<span class="scenario-rating-max">/10</span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="scenario-rating">
              <span class="scenario-rating-label">Yungas</span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-bar yungas"><span class="scenario-bar-fill yungas" style="width:55%"></span></span>
              <span class="scenario-rating-value accent">5.5<span class="scenario-rating-max">/10</span></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="scenario-rank">#13 of 17</div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider-accent"></div>

  <!-- Composite Rankings Table -->
  <section class="py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <div class="mb-14">
        <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 reveal">Composite Country Rankings</h2>
        <p class="text-bark-500 mt-3 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="100">
          All six scenarios weighted equally (16.7% each). Bolivia ranks #7 &mdash; honest, not inflated.
          The real story is in the variance.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto reveal" data-delay="200">
        <table class="rankings-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th class="rank-col">#</th>
              <th class="country-col">Country</th>
              <th>Nuclear</th>
              <th>Sea</th>
              <th>Digital</th>
              <th>Trust</th>
              <th>Resources</th>
              <th>Pandemic</th>
              <th class="composite-col">Composite</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td class="rank-cell">1</td>
              <td class="country-cell">New Zealand</td>
              <td>9.2</td><td>8.0</td><td>7.3</td><td>6.8</td><td>8.5</td><td>9.0</td>
              <td class="composite-cell">8.13</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="rank-cell">2</td>
              <td class="country-cell">Uruguay</td>
              <td>8.5</td><td>8.7</td><td>7.0</td><td>6.5</td><td>8.3</td><td>7.3</td>
              <td class="composite-cell">7.72</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="rank-cell">3</td>
              <td class="country-cell">Iceland</td>
              <td>7.8</td><td>7.3</td><td>6.8</td><td>7.0</td><td>8.0</td><td>8.5</td>
              <td class="composite-cell">7.57</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="rank-cell">4</td>
              <td class="country-cell">Switzerland</td>
              <td>6.3</td><td>9.0</td><td>7.5</td><td>7.3</td><td>7.5</td><td>6.8</td>
              <td class="composite-cell">7.40</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="rank-cell">5</td>
              <td class="country-cell">Bhutan</td>
              <td>5.8</td><td>6.3</td><td>8.2</td><td>8.7</td><td>6.8</td><td>7.0</td>
              <td class="composite-cell">7.13</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="rank-cell">6</td>
              <td class="country-cell">Paraguay</td>
              <td>7.5</td><td>8.3</td><td>7.8</td><td>7.5</td><td>6.5</td><td>4.8</td>
              <td class="composite-cell">7.07</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="highlight-row">
              <td class="rank-cell">7</td>
              <td class="country-cell">Bolivia</td>
              <td>6.5</td><td>7.5</td><td class="high-cell">8.5</td><td class="high-cell">9.0</td><td class="low-cell">5.0</td><td class="low-cell">5.0</td>
              <td class="composite-cell">6.92</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="rank-cell">8</td>
              <td class="country-cell">Costa Rica</td>
              <td>7.0</td><td>6.8</td><td>6.5</td><td>6.3</td><td>7.8</td><td>6.3</td>
              <td class="composite-cell">6.78</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="rank-cell">9</td>
              <td class="country-cell">Tasmania</td>
              <td>8.8</td><td>5.5</td><td>6.0</td><td>5.5</td><td>5.8</td><td>8.3</td>
              <td class="composite-cell">6.65</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="rank-cell">10</td>
              <td class="country-cell">Patagonia</td>
              <td>8.0</td><td>7.8</td><td>6.3</td><td>5.5</td><td>6.3</td><td>5.5</td>
              <td class="composite-cell">6.57</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="text-bark-400 text-sm mt-4 reveal" data-delay="300">
        Full 17-country analysis available. Countries 11&ndash;17: Ireland (5.97), Norway (5.88), Chile (5.85), Fiji (5.67), Portugal (5.23), Georgia (4.97), Armenia (4.08).
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Where Bolivia Wins — Dark Section -->
  <section class="section-dark py-28 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <div class="mb-16">
        <span class="text-label text-accent tracking-[0.2em]">Pattern Recognition</span>
        <h2 class="text-headline text-bark-50 mt-3 reveal">Where Bolivia Wins</h2>
        <p class="text-bark-400 mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[1.1rem] leading-[1.85] reveal" data-delay="100">
          Bolivia dominates the scenarios where disconnection and community cohesion matter more
          than infrastructure &mdash; trust crisis, digital attack, sea logistics. The crises where
          being offline is a liability? Bolivia struggles there too.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 mb-16">
        <div class="reveal" data-delay="150">
          <div class="text-[3rem] font-display font-bold text-accent leading-none">#1</div>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-100 mt-2 text-lg">Trust Crisis</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-400 text-[0.95rem] mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            Ayllu governance is structurally immune to deepfakes. Face-to-face reciprocity
            cannot be manipulated by synthetic media. 500+ years of proven resilience
            against institutional collapse.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal" data-delay="250">
          <div class="text-[3rem] font-display font-bold text-accent leading-none">#1</div>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-100 mt-2 text-lg">Digital Attack</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-400 text-[0.95rem] mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            Only 70.2% internet penetration nationally, 38% rural. Cash economy dominant.
            Radio widely used. The informal economy &mdash; 80% of Bolivia's total &mdash;
            barely touches digital infrastructure.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal" data-delay="350">
          <div class="text-[3rem] font-display font-bold text-accent leading-none">#6</div>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-100 mt-2 text-lg">Sea Logistics</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-400 text-[0.95rem] mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            Landlocked, usually a weakness, becomes strategic when sea trade collapses.
            Overland routes to five neighbors. Family farming produces 88% of the food
            basket without imported inputs.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Key quote — the variance insight -->
      <blockquote class="border-l-3 border-ember pl-8 py-6 max-w-3xl reveal" data-delay="200">
        <p class="font-display text-bark-100 text-[1.2rem] md:text-[1.4rem] leading-[1.5] font-medium">
          Bolivia has the widest variance of any country evaluated &mdash; ranging from #1 to #14
          depending on scenario. This is not a safe country. It is a country where the specific
          things that are unsafe are the specific things a community can address.
        </p>
      </blockquote>

      <!-- Variance visualization -->
      <div class="mt-16 reveal" data-delay="300">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-200 text-sm tracking-[0.1em] uppercase mb-6">Bolivia's Ranking by Scenario</h3>
        <div class="variance-chart">
          <div class="variance-row">
            <span class="variance-label">Trust Crisis</span>
            <div class="variance-track"><div class="variance-marker" style="left:calc((1/17)*100%)"><span class="variance-pos">#1</span></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="variance-row">
            <span class="variance-label">Digital Attack</span>
            <div class="variance-track"><div class="variance-marker" style="left:calc((1/17)*100%)"><span class="variance-pos">#1</span></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="variance-row">
            <span class="variance-label">Sea Logistics</span>
            <div class="variance-track"><div class="variance-marker" style="left:calc((6/17)*100%)"><span class="variance-pos">#6</span></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="variance-row">
            <span class="variance-label">Nuclear</span>
            <div class="variance-track"><div class="variance-marker mid" style="left:calc((9/17)*100%)"><span class="variance-pos">#9</span></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="variance-row">
            <span class="variance-label">Pandemic</span>
            <div class="variance-track"><div class="variance-marker low" style="left:calc((13/17)*100%)"><span class="variance-pos">#13</span></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="variance-row">
            <span class="variance-label">Resource Wars</span>
            <div class="variance-track"><div class="variance-marker low" style="left:calc((14/17)*100%)"><span class="variance-pos">#14</span></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-between text-[0.65rem] text-bark-500 mt-2 font-display tracking-wider uppercase">
          <span>Best</span>
          <span>Worst</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider-accent"></div>

  <!-- Trust Crisis Deep Dive -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <div class="mb-16 max-w-3xl">
        <span class="text-label text-accent tracking-[0.2em]">Deep Dive</span>
        <h2 class="text-headline text-bark-800 mt-3 reveal">The Trust Crisis Angle</h2>
        <p class="text-bark-500 mt-4 text-[1.1rem] leading-[1.85] reveal" data-delay="100">
          This scenario deserves its own section because it is not hypothetical. It is already underway.
          Deepfake fraud exceeded $410M in the first half of 2025. Forrester projects $40B annually by 2027.
          The WEF rates misinformation as the #1 global short-term risk for the second year running.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Trust crisis sub-sections -->
      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 lg:gap-16">

        <div class="reveal" data-delay="150">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-xl mb-4">
            Physical Communities Resist Manipulation
          </h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 leading-[1.85] mb-4">
            Trust is a physical phenomenon evolved for face-to-face groups of 50&ndash;150 people.
            Digital institutions tried to scale trust beyond this limit through reputation systems,
            institutional authority, cryptographic verification, and legal frameworks. Every one
            of these mechanisms is <em>mediated</em> &mdash; requiring intermediaries that can be
            compromised, corrupted, or deepfaked.
          </p>
          <p class="text-bark-600 leading-[1.85]">
            Physical communities bypass mediation entirely. You know your neighbor because you see
            them every day, not because a platform verifies their identity. You trust the baker
            because you ate the bread, not because of a 4.8-star review.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal" data-delay="250">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-xl mb-4">
            Ayllu Governance: Structurally Immune
          </h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 leading-[1.85] mb-4">
            The ayllu &mdash; the traditional community governance unit of Quechua and Aymara peoples &mdash;
            has features that cannot be attacked by the mechanisms eroding modern institutions:
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-3">
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="text-accent font-display font-bold text-sm mt-0.5 shrink-0">01</span>
              <span class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-bark-800">Rotating authority (thakhi)</strong> &mdash; Leadership rotates annually. Every family serves. Deepfaking a leader has no long-term value.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="text-accent font-display font-bold text-sm mt-0.5 shrink-0">02</span>
              <span class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-bark-800">Reciprocal labor (ayni)</strong> &mdash; Trust built through accumulated physical labor, not digital reputation. The community IS the ledger.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="text-accent font-display font-bold text-sm mt-0.5 shrink-0">03</span>
              <span class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-bark-800">Collective projects (mink'a)</strong> &mdash; Free-rider detection is automatic. Physical absence is visible. No contractor fraud when the community watches the work.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="text-accent font-display font-bold text-sm mt-0.5 shrink-0">04</span>
              <span class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-bark-800">Consensus assembly</strong> &mdash; Decisions require physical gathering. Disinformation must survive real-time community interrogation.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal" data-delay="350">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-xl mb-4">
            Low Digital Penetration as a Feature
          </h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 leading-[1.85] mb-4">
            Bolivia's 70.2% internet penetration (38% rural) is typically presented as a development failure.
            In a trust crisis, it becomes the country's single most valuable statistic.
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem]">
            <li class="pl-4 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.5em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              <strong class="text-bark-800">Smaller deepfake attack surface</strong> &mdash; 62% of the rural population is unreachable by digital manipulation campaigns
            </li>
            <li class="pl-4 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.5em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              <strong class="text-bark-800">No &ldquo;information shock&rdquo;</strong> &mdash; countries at 95%+ internet face a terrifying transition when digital trust collapses; Bolivia's rural communities face none
            </li>
            <li class="pl-4 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.5em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
